# Trivy CVE Ignore List — AgentShroud Gateway
#
# IEC 62443 SR 2.4 / FR 2 (Use Control) risk assessment:
# Each entry below has been reviewed and accepted per the criteria:
#   - Not reachable from external input
#   - Component is vendor-internal / non-exposed
#   - Practical exploitability is negligible in this deployment context
#
# Review cadence: reassess at each minor version bump of the affected package.
#
# ── SCRUM-101 (2026-07-14): ZERO active suppressions. ──────────────────────────
# The sole prior entry, CVE-2021-23358 (Prototype Pollution in `underscore` embedded
# in Wazuh Agent 4.9.2's internal node_modules), was RETIRED — not by suppression, but
# by upgrading Wazuh Agent 4.9.2 → 4.14.5, which ships underscore >= 1.13. A rescan of
# both the gateway and openclaw images (trivy, CRITICAL+HIGH) confirms CVE-2021-23358 is
# no longer present. AgentShroud now carries NO accepted/ignored container CVEs.
#
# Any future entry MUST document: CVE id, exact location, IEC 62443 SR 2.4 reachability
# analysis, and why no upstream fix exists — the same standard applied above.
